WEBVTT

00:00:02.718 --> 00:00:06.722
We can 't even use GPs or
commercial satellite connections.

00:00:06.931 --> 00:00:08.390
What's going on?

00:00:08.599 --> 00:00:12.978
This is a global phenomenon.
lt isn 't just our own satellites.

00:00:13.187 --> 00:00:18.234
Navstar, Comstar, and other
spy satellites are being badly affected.

00:00:18.442 --> 00:00:20.528
There is no telling when they' ll be restored.

00:00:20.736 --> 00:00:24.490
It's solar wind.
And on a scale very seldom <i>seen.</i>

00:00:24.698 --> 00:00:26.367
Solar wind?

00:00:27.368 --> 00:00:28.452
Are we sure of that?

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.538
This interference most likely is caused

00:00:30.746 --> 00:00:33.582
by strong electromagnetic waves from the sun.

00:00:33.791 --> 00:00:36.919
It was reported that there was
an increase in sunspot activity

00:00:37.127 --> 00:00:39.255
over the past few days.

00:00:39.463 --> 00:00:42.716
Even so, is it possible for it
to cause this much damage?

00:00:42.925 --> 00:00:44.051
I 'm not sure, sir.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.179
All l know is, it's an exceedingly
rare case in recorded history.

00:00:47.388 --> 00:00:48.973
Rare, eh?

00:00:49.181 --> 00:00:51.767
I have experience with heavy storms.

00:00:51.976 --> 00:00:56.814
When natural disasters like this strike,
neither side feels like waging war.

00:00:57.022 --> 00:01:01.318
But the enemy's taken advantage of this.
<i>That</i> is the problem.

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:05.197
True. Accurate predictions
are supposed to be impossible.

00:01:05.406 --> 00:01:06.740
Normally.

00:01:06.949 --> 00:01:09.285
What are your thoughts,
Lieutenant Commander?

00:01:10.911 --> 00:01:15.666
Yes sir, for now...
we can only remain on guard.

00:01:15.874 --> 00:01:19.378
I 'm already aware of that.
But in your opinion...

00:01:20.921 --> 00:01:24.216
lncoming ultrahigh-speed cruise missiles.

00:01:24.425 --> 00:01:27.052
Eight of them, in sector D4!

00:01:27.261 --> 00:01:31.390
Range, 70 miles. Mach 6.3.
Sixty-five seconds to impact.

00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:33.767
Intercept! Go to Red 1 !

00:01:33.976 --> 00:01:36.478
Order personnel at surface
observation posts to evacuate!

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:39.898
Air traffic control.

00:01:40.107 --> 00:01:42.651
Gebo 6 is to abandon craft
on the runway and take shelter.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.445
As are all nearby base personnel.

00:01:44.653 --> 00:01:47.781
Y-Yes, ma 'am. And Gebo 5, who's taxiing?

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:49.074
Emergency takeoff.

00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:51.827
Withdraw west of Merida lsland,
and stand by in the air!

00:01:52.036 --> 00:01:53.037
Yes, ma 'am.

00:01:53.245 --> 00:01:56.123
PCO reports interceptor missiles
are being launched!

00:02:00.711 --> 00:02:02.796
Alert, Red 1 .

00:02:03.005 --> 00:02:05.841
Alert, Red 1 . All surface personnel,

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.510
abandon your work and
take shelter underground!

00:02:16.852 --> 00:02:20.564
Interceptor missiles, making contact. 2, 1 ...

00:02:22.232 --> 00:02:23.942
Three missiles successfully intercepted.

00:02:24.151 --> 00:02:26.570
The remaining five are inbound.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.822
Second wave of enemy missiles detected!

00:02:29.031 --> 00:02:33.952
Sector E4! Nine--No, 1 2 of them!
Range, 85 miles!

00:02:34.161 --> 00:02:36.080
BOL, intercept with all missiles!

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:40.334
Yes, ma 'am. Launching all missiles
from #6 to #9 using BOL.

00:02:42.961 --> 00:02:45.589
T-Ten seconds until the first wave impacts!

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.091
Remain calm!

00:02:50.761 --> 00:02:52.471
If they're nuclear, it will be instantaneous.

00:03:09.405 --> 00:03:20.999
<i>I wonder why we were 5orn into this world</i>

00:03:21.875 --> 00:03:29.091
<i>Even though Iove is always there next to me</i>

00:03:29.299 --> 00:03:33.470
<i>I kept Iooking away in my indecision</i>

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:43.355
No <i>matter what strong iron armor
I try to protect</i> you <i>with,</i>

00:03:43.564 --> 00:03:50.154
<i>I wonder if I'm a5Ie to protect your heart as well</i>

00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:52.573
<i>Even if dreams remain dreams</i>

00:03:52.781 --> 00:03:56.326
<i>Even if the game 's over I won 't give up</i>

00:03:56.535 --> 00:04:00.706
<i>If I reach</i> out so <i>that</i> you <i>can always 5e</i>

00:04:00.914 --> 00:04:02.416
<i>the way</i> you <i>are</i>

00:04:02.624 --> 00:04:08.839
<i>AII</i> our <i>nows and thens will start to shine</i>

00:04:09.047 --> 00:04:15.596
Your <i>smile, that's my dream,
even in a world of darkness</i>

00:04:26.148 --> 00:04:30.277
" Episode 2
Damage Control "

00:04:31.653 --> 00:04:34.656
Lie low on the seat. Do <i>not</i> sit up.

00:04:34.865 --> 00:04:36.074
Wh-What's going on?

00:04:36.283 --> 00:04:37.910
Enemies. We' re running for it.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:40.996
Stay down!

00:05:20.744 --> 00:05:21.829
Sousuke, up top!

00:05:46.937 --> 00:05:48.564
Chidori! Are you hurt?

00:05:48.772 --> 00:05:49.857
I 'm all right.

00:05:55.445 --> 00:05:56.530
Stay down!

00:06:02.828 --> 00:06:04.621
Sh-Should l shoot?

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:05.956
--No.
--But...

00:06:06.164 --> 00:06:07.457
Don 't touch the gun!

00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:10.252
Don 't shoot.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:11.962
Sousuke...?

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:15.215
You mustn't... shoot.

00:06:16.633 --> 00:06:19.303
"Cool Home Delivery"

00:06:19.303 --> 00:06:19.344
"Cool Home Delivery" They fled to the
west. Towards Nogawa Park, along Route 1 4.

00:06:19.344 --> 00:06:22.806
They fled to the west.
Towards Nogawa Park, along Route 1 4.

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:24.433
Keep chasing them.

00:06:24.641 --> 00:06:25.475
Can we open fire?

00:06:25.684 --> 00:06:27.477
Whatever, fire away.

00:06:27.686 --> 00:06:28.812
Roger that.

00:07:14.149 --> 00:07:15.275
Sousuke, up ahead!

00:07:24.368 --> 00:07:25.494
Chidori?

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:29.456
Chidori!

00:07:31.249 --> 00:07:33.043
H-Hey, buddy.

00:07:33.251 --> 00:07:34.294
You okay?

00:07:34.503 --> 00:07:35.629
Move!

00:07:41.051 --> 00:07:41.927
Can you stand?

00:07:42.135 --> 00:07:43.261
Think so.

00:07:44.596 --> 00:07:45.389
Can you run?

00:07:45.597 --> 00:07:46.682
I 'll manage.

00:07:52.145 --> 00:07:55.732
I 'll never let you...
drive me anywhere again.

00:07:55.941 --> 00:07:58.986
Sorry, but you will any number of times
if it's for your protection!

00:08:02.781 --> 00:08:04.825
Innocent people got caught up in this!

00:08:05.033 --> 00:08:06.451
All we can do right now is run.

00:08:08.829 --> 00:08:11.456
Uruz 7 to Gebo 9, can you hear me?

00:08:11.665 --> 00:08:15.794
Gebo 9 <i>here.</i> Report your situation, Uruz 7.

00:08:16.003 --> 00:08:18.255
Uruz 7 is currently engaging
the enemy in combat.

00:08:18.463 --> 00:08:20.298
Heading northwest on foot.

00:08:20.507 --> 00:08:23.593
Gebo 9, roger. Any change in the LZ?

00:08:23.802 --> 00:08:26.096
No change. The smoke bomb will be yellow.

00:08:26.304 --> 00:08:28.056
At the park 500m to the <i>west...</i>

00:08:49.619 --> 00:08:50.996
Get up!

00:08:51.204 --> 00:08:52.330
Run!

00:08:56.209 --> 00:08:57.419
Oh, my god...

00:08:59.046 --> 00:09:00.213
Are you o--

00:09:00.422 --> 00:09:01.339
He's hurt because of us!

00:09:01.548 --> 00:09:02.632
Don 't stop! Don 't think about it!

00:09:02.841 --> 00:09:04.176
Sousuke!

00:09:06.344 --> 00:09:07.554
Sorry...

00:09:15.479 --> 00:09:17.064
l can 't run anymore!

00:09:17.272 --> 00:09:18.815
Just a little more! Keep trying!

00:09:23.487 --> 00:09:25.489
We' ll wait here for the chopper. Stay down.

00:09:25.697 --> 00:09:26.239
But...

00:09:26.448 --> 00:09:27.574
Keep down!

00:09:45.592 --> 00:09:46.718
They on our side?

00:09:46.927 --> 00:09:48.011
They got here in time!

00:09:55.685 --> 00:09:56.770
That's the way.

00:09:59.898 --> 00:10:03.151
Come around to the north side.
l 'll bring you in from the rear!

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:04.736
Get up, let's go!

00:10:28.093 --> 00:10:29.177
Damn it!

00:10:31.221 --> 00:10:32.597
No! No more!

00:10:32.806 --> 00:10:33.431
Don 't give up!

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:35.016
No!

00:10:35.225 --> 00:10:36.351
Get down!

00:10:44.609 --> 00:10:45.819
My ammo...

00:10:48.572 --> 00:10:52.367
Activating emergency evacuation mode,

00:10:52.576 --> 00:10:54.786
based on special instructions
found in file X-ray 1 .

00:10:54.995 --> 00:10:57.539
Mandatory use of external audio is in effect.

00:10:57.747 --> 00:10:59.082
Is that...

00:10:59.291 --> 00:11:06.047
This is serial number C-002.
Code name, ARX-7 Arbalest.

00:11:06.256 --> 00:11:08.383
If any officers of the
affiliated forces are nearby,

00:11:08.592 --> 00:11:11.052
please respond verbally.

00:11:11.261 --> 00:11:12.762
Al! You 're alive?

00:11:12.971 --> 00:11:16.766
Check. ldentity confirmed as
Sergeant Sousuke Sagara.

00:11:16.975 --> 00:11:19.436
Affirmative, Uruz 7.
This unit is being exposed

00:11:19.644 --> 00:11:22.981
to heat that <i>exceeds</i>
the threshold for practical use.

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:24.608
Permission to seek safety?

00:11:24.816 --> 00:11:27.110
Permission granted! Get over here right now!

00:11:27.319 --> 00:11:28.403
Roger.

00:11:48.715 --> 00:11:50.300
Chidori! Climb on!

00:11:56.765 --> 00:11:58.391
S-Sto...

00:12:10.445 --> 00:12:12.822
Give me a hand!
Somebody else is down over here!

00:12:13.031 --> 00:12:13.698
Are they conscious?

00:12:13.907 --> 00:12:16.660
I don 't know! l called out
but they don't respond!

00:12:17.661 --> 00:12:18.870
What are our casualties?

00:12:19.079 --> 00:12:23.583
Minor injuries, 28.
Serious injuries, 11 . Deceased, 5.

00:12:23.792 --> 00:12:26.544
Observation post 2 personnel
didn't evacuate in time.

00:12:29.089 --> 00:12:30.006
I <i>see.</i>

00:12:30.215 --> 00:12:34.427
Our problems are only beginning.
That was a preliminary attack.

00:12:34.636 --> 00:12:36.012
Landing forces?

00:12:36.221 --> 00:12:37.305
They'll come.

00:12:38.306 --> 00:12:40.308
Make no mistake. They'll be airborne.

00:12:40.517 --> 00:12:42.477
This is Gebo 5.

00:12:42.686 --> 00:12:44.604
Calling Merida lsland command center.

00:12:44.813 --> 00:12:47.482
Group of large aircraft detected.
Over ten of them.

00:12:47.691 --> 00:12:49.776
Approaching from sector P8.

00:12:54.906 --> 00:12:56.700
Send out Super Harriers to intercept them.

00:12:56.908 --> 00:12:57.867
Yes, ma 'am!

00:12:58.076 --> 00:13:00.620
Lieutenant Commander,
do you think we can fully hold them off?

00:13:00.829 --> 00:13:03.415
Possibly, with our usual strength.

00:13:03.623 --> 00:13:07.585
But in this situation, we' re practically blind.

00:13:07.794 --> 00:13:10.547
The front door is demolished, too.

00:13:10.755 --> 00:13:14.634
In the worst case, we might have to
consider how the crew will escape.

00:13:14.843 --> 00:13:15.927
Yes, ma 'am.

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:18.680
What shape is the runway in?

00:13:18.888 --> 00:13:21.891
We can send up Super Harriers,
but definitely not transports.

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:24.394
Repairs would probably require three days.

00:13:28.732 --> 00:13:29.774
What about the <i>Danaan?</i>

00:13:29.983 --> 00:13:33.320
The <i>Tuatha de Danaan</i> could
transport everyone on this base.

00:13:33.528 --> 00:13:35.572
But as you 're aware,

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:38.074
it's been undergoing maintenance
since last <i>week.</i>

00:13:38.283 --> 00:13:42.078
It will take more than half a day
before it can put out to sea.

00:13:42.287 --> 00:13:43.455
Have them hurry.

00:13:43.663 --> 00:13:46.041
Mr. Mardukas, go take command
of the work personally.

00:13:46.249 --> 00:13:47.667
Understood, ma 'am.

00:13:49.794 --> 00:13:51.171
Mr. Kalinin.

00:13:51.379 --> 00:13:53.548
Please have every AS ready to go.

00:13:53.757 --> 00:13:56.301
All of them, including the M6s
we use for training.

00:13:56.509 --> 00:13:58.219
Deploy them on the north coast,
with D equipment.

00:13:58.428 --> 00:13:59.137
Understood, ma 'am.

00:13:59.346 --> 00:14:01.014
Just a moment!

00:14:01.222 --> 00:14:03.224
Gebo 5 has an additional report.

00:14:03.433 --> 00:14:04.517
Put him through.

00:14:05.935 --> 00:14:07.145
This is Gebo 5.

00:14:07.354 --> 00:14:11.691
Some kind of, uh, heat sources
detected at sea in sector G2.

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:15.862
They number three.
l suspect they're underwater vessels.

00:14:16.071 --> 00:14:19.491
Deliver your report clearly.
What is it that's coming?

00:14:19.699 --> 00:14:23.078
I apologize. They simply don 't
fall into any known category.

00:14:23.286 --> 00:14:27.082
I just picked them up on optical sensors!
Sending you the image.

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:31.961
What in the world...?

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:33.630
They're Behemoths.

00:15:04.994 --> 00:15:06.079
What the...?

00:15:08.665 --> 00:15:10.291
Behemoths?

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:13.753
Yeah, like the one you guys
tangled with in Tokyo.

00:15:13.962 --> 00:15:15.422
There's three of them.

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:17.132
Por real?

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:18.383
Is that bad news?

00:15:18.591 --> 00:15:24.264
Very bad. Missiles and 57mm cannons
didn't work against that giant AS.

00:15:24.472 --> 00:15:28.726
How does our captain expect us
to fight against monsters like that?

00:15:28.935 --> 00:15:31.187
Complaining won 't help us.

00:15:31.396 --> 00:15:34.315
I don 't like this. At <i>all.</i>

00:15:34.524 --> 00:15:36.818
It's fine if you skip everything
before process C!

00:15:37.026 --> 00:15:37.444
Yes, sir!

00:15:37.652 --> 00:15:39.446
Carry the 40mm rounds over there!

00:15:39.654 --> 00:15:41.322
--Load all the GECs at site 2!

00:15:41.322 --> 00:15:43.408
--AS operators, assemble!
--Load all the GECs at site 2!

00:15:45.785 --> 00:15:46.953
You 're all here?

00:15:47.162 --> 00:15:51.249
As you probably know,
Amalgam has launched a major offensive.

00:15:51.458 --> 00:15:53.835
The three Behemoths pose
a particularly major threat.

00:15:54.043 --> 00:15:56.254
They're due to make landfall in 40 minutes.

00:15:57.422 --> 00:16:00.133
The radio interference
allowed them to get close,

00:16:00.341 --> 00:16:02.051
but it's up to us to intercept them.

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:03.761
" Intercept, " huh?

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:07.223
Aren 't those giants equipped
with those Lambda Driver things?

00:16:07.432 --> 00:16:11.227
That's right. Regular attacks won 't work at all.

00:16:11.436 --> 00:16:14.564
I 've read the report. This is ill-advised.

00:16:14.772 --> 00:16:17.358
Even so, we have to confront them.

00:16:17.567 --> 00:16:20.820
This base is strong against bombardment,
but there's a limit.

00:16:21.029 --> 00:16:22.989
The <i>de Danaan</i>'s in the middle of maintenance.

00:16:23.198 --> 00:16:26.034
If three Behemoths come ashore,
they' ll destroy it eventually.

00:16:26.242 --> 00:16:26.951
Yeah, but--

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:29.120
It's our only means of escape.

00:16:30.747 --> 00:16:32.874
This is a solitary island far out at sea.

00:16:33.082 --> 00:16:38.338
If we lose the <i>de Danaan,</i>
we'll all wind up dead in this cave.

00:16:38.546 --> 00:16:42.342
There's no way to survive
other than defeating those Behemoths.

00:16:43.885 --> 00:16:45.970
How about this, then?

00:16:46.179 --> 00:16:48.556
Stop fighting this losing battle.

00:16:48.765 --> 00:16:52.352
How about we take some rifles
and go to the command center?

00:16:54.646 --> 00:16:56.564
Stop it, Speck!

00:16:56.773 --> 00:16:59.567
I bet if we handed over Tessa
and the <i>de Danaan</i> unharmed,

00:16:59.776 --> 00:17:01.694
the enemy would go for it.

00:17:01.903 --> 00:17:06.449
I think they'd be happy to
settle this with a businesslike agreement.

00:17:06.658 --> 00:17:11.704
Go on, keep saying that crap.
l 'll consider it treason.

00:17:11.913 --> 00:17:16.292
Come on, l ' m just a hired gun.

00:17:16.501 --> 00:17:21.256
Are you telling me to happily die
for my team? Por my comrades?

00:17:21.464 --> 00:17:23.299
You son of a...

00:17:23.508 --> 00:17:29.180
l don 't want to waste my life,
for the record. Don 't you all agree?

00:17:29.389 --> 00:17:30.807
I did warn you.

00:17:31.015 --> 00:17:33.268
Corporal Speck, l hereby sentence you to--

00:17:33.476 --> 00:17:37.605
You 'd sell me out?
That's a rather fine idea.

00:17:37.814 --> 00:17:39.440
Captain.

00:17:39.649 --> 00:17:43.820
I suspected that topic might come up,
so l came to check on you.

00:17:44.028 --> 00:17:48.157
You were listening? Well, it's nothing personal.

00:17:48.366 --> 00:17:50.118
Please let me have your side arm.

00:17:59.043 --> 00:17:59.961
Tessa!

00:18:00.169 --> 00:18:03.881
Some of you are probably inclined
to agree with Mr. Speck.

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:05.592
But l won't allow it.

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:09.429
If anyone is contemplating treason,
l 'll shoot you to death right <i>here.</i>

00:18:09.637 --> 00:18:14.017
Whoa, be reasonable. l think
you 're a great girl and all, but--

00:18:23.151 --> 00:18:25.445
Reconsider your attitude, Corporal.

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:29.616
Perhaps you thought l was going
to come all the way here

00:18:29.824 --> 00:18:33.328
to beg you to cooperate
with tears in my eyes?

00:18:34.746 --> 00:18:39.125
That l 'd ask for a mix of sympathy and loyalty,
banking on your commendable goodwill?

00:18:40.752 --> 00:18:45.214
Doesn't the fact that you 're here mean that
you, too, walk the path of the warrior?

00:18:45.423 --> 00:18:49.677
You arrived at this predicament
via your own will. Am l wrong?

00:18:51.137 --> 00:18:54.307
Did you think l was some
princess in name only?

00:18:55.933 --> 00:18:57.143
No.

00:18:57.352 --> 00:19:00.355
Tell me who l am!

00:19:05.401 --> 00:19:07.820
Captain Teletha Testarossa.

00:19:08.905 --> 00:19:12.325
Commanding officer of
the <i>Tuatha de Danaan</i>'s forces.

00:19:12.533 --> 00:19:16.996
Then take back your previous
remarks and apologize.

00:19:17.205 --> 00:19:18.539
Immediately.

00:19:20.375 --> 00:19:23.795
I take it back. l apologize.

00:19:25.004 --> 00:19:26.089
Very well.

00:19:31.302 --> 00:19:35.807
Mr. Speck. Your team is in need of your skills.

00:19:36.015 --> 00:19:41.062
I will overlook your treasonous instigation
once we all survive this.

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:45.483
Survive? How do you figure
that's going to happen?

00:19:45.692 --> 00:19:48.486
You seem to have the wrong idea.

00:19:48.695 --> 00:19:53.074
I have never once ordered any of you to " die. "

00:19:53.282 --> 00:19:56.536
I never have, and l never will.

